  "body": "## What changed\n\nWas stacked on #401 (#317). That PR has merged, so this branch has origin/main merged in and targets `main`.\n\n- **Rest crosses setups where the body is carried.** A Setup2 op that reads the program ahead (a Pocket3D or MultiAxisRough rest mask, the verify prior used by the rapid, reach and top-stock laws) now reads what Setup1 cut. The rest grid is the origin setup's block. Each setup's cut moves are swept into it, and the body is carried at every boundary through `stock_sim::carry::entry` + `Body::carry`, which is the same call the program sim makes (`crates/app/src/rest/across.rs`, new).\n- **Clip-entered setups keep their own block.** Two setups that hold the part the same way and are not linked are entered by the M3.2 A clip. Rest there still starts from the setup's own block, as before. It is not yet stated whether that setup gets a fresh blank or the same part (#320), and the fresh block never assumes material is gone.\n- **Staleness.** When the chain crosses a setup boundary, the rest digest adds the setups it crosses, each lattice turn and the origin setup's stock to the predecessors' path digest. So any of these stales the later op: regenerating a Setup1 op, re-aligning, linking or unlinking a setup, a Setup1 stock edit, a deletion or a reorder. Undo un-stales it. `stale_reason` names the predecessor and the carry.\n- **Suppressed-ahead refusal** (`rest::suppressed_cuts_ahead`, #161) walks the same chain, so a suppressed Setup1 cut refuses the Setup2 op at the post by name.\n- `operation::write_setup_stock` and `carry::first_body` are now `pub(crate)`. `rest.rs` was split, with the pilot and turned readings moved to `rest/pilots.rs` (400-line law).\n\n## Refused by name\n\n- **A carry the lattice refuses** (side-on turns, Z turns off the quarter, lathe or mill-turn). Every `reads_prior` op in the receiving setup is refused at `collect_job` with `REST_CARRY_REFUSAL` plus the carry's own reason, which names both setups. It is never generated against a fresh block.\n- Left for #319, unchanged here: raw-stock convictions in a later setup still read that setup's declared block. The carried prior only *acquits*, and only where the carried body really is cut. Convicting against carried material that stands outside the declared block is #319's job. `drills_ahead` and `turned_ahead` stay same-setup; they are lathe-only, and the carry is refused on a lathe.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/318-rest-across-setups.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Setup2 linked \"Same as\" Setup1: Rest2's path is bit-identical to the same op's path when both ops sit in one setup. With the clip (not linked), Rest2 re-cuts the pocket Rough1 cleared, and its cutting length below the stock top is strictly larger.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/rest_across_setups.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n  - `a_second_setup_rest_pass_skips_what_the_first_setup_cleared`\n  - `a_change_ahead_in_the_first_setup_stales_the_second_setups_rest_and_undo_restores_it`\n  - `a_suppressed_first_setup_cut_refuses_the_second_setups_rest_by_name`\n  - `a_clip_entered_setup_does_not_read_the_first_setups_cuts`\n  - `a_carry_the_lattice_refuses_refuses_the_rest_reading_by_name`\n- `setup_carry::a_turn_the_lattice_cannot_carry_is_refused_by_name`: the refusal now arrives earlier, at Face2's generation, and names the carry. Before, it only reached the program sim.\n\n## Gate (on the tree merged with current main)\n\n- app: lib (95), rest_across_setups (5), remachining (6), suppressed_rest (2), setup_carry (5), setup_relative (8), setups (11), setup_align (9), posting (17), golden_cl (23, goldens unchanged), operations (117 + 6 ignored), drill_prior (12), drill_prior_kinds (4), drilling_axial (7), stock_stamp (4), stock_sim_document (9), lathe_field_sim (6): all green\n- clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app and camcraft-sim, all targets: clean. The sim crate is not touched.\n\nChangelog: Rest machining in a later setup reads the stock carried from earlier setups (rest passes skip material already removed), an upstream change marks the later setup's operations Stale, and a carry the lattice cannot hold refuses the rest-reading operation by name.\n\nFixes #318\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
